    "evidence_text": "PLoS Med 4(9): e278.\n\nAllele A refers to the susceptibility alleles as given in column seven.\n\nUltrasound imaging for lumbar punctures and epidural catheterisations: systematic review and meta-analysis.\n\nFive studies evaluated lumbar punctures and nine evaluated epidural catheterisations.\n\nUltrasound may be a useful adjunct for these procedures.\n\nRESULTS 249 errors were identified.\n\nCONCLUSIONS The rate of intravenous drug errors was high.\n\nDESIGN A retrospective study.   \n\n\nSETTING National referral hospital.   \n\n\nThe effectiveness of right heart catheterization in the initial care of critically ill patients. SUPPORT Investigators.\n\nThese findings were all confirmed by multivariable modeling techniques.\n\nThe cause of this apparent lack of benefit is unclear.\n\nEffect of clinical guidelines on medical practice: a systematic review of rigorous evaluations.\n\nHowever, the size of the improvements in performance varied considerably.\n\nExtravasation injuries on regional neonatal units.\n\nDATA SYNTHESIS We found 15 randomized trials.\n\nRole of Computerized Physician Order Entry Systems in Facilitating Medication Errors\n\nThe premise was that simply notifying the physician would increase the use of appropriate prophylactic measures.\n\nThere are 2 lessons urologists can learn from this study.",
